window.docContents[25].resolve({"/Storage-and-commands/Loops/#Core-C______--Storage-and-commands--Loops":{"contents":"The rule While-T recurs on its own conclusion. A return in the body interrupts the loop. The divergence of while (true) {} has no derivation, a limitation of inductive big step semantics (Kahn, RR-0601, §4.4, p. 11).The implementations are partial, so Lean records opaque constants that carry the type and not the body, and no property of them is proved here.\n\nThe for is defined through while. The variable of the initialiser has the loop as its scope, the body is a block of its own, and the step runs after the body, outside the body's scope.The implementations are partial, so Lean records opaque constants that carry the type and not the body, and no property of them is proved here.\n\n","context":"Core C++\u0009Storage and commands","header":"4.6. Loops","id":"/Storage-and-commands/Loops/#Core-C______--Storage-and-commands--Loops"}});